  "notes": [
    "Names: English from the ESPN team feed and spl.com.sa/en/teams (SPL itself writes 'Diriyah Club'; ESPN, SPA and the rules use 'Al Diriyah'); Arabic from spl.com.sa/ar/teams, matching Sabq's King's Cup round-of-32 list.",
    "Codes follow ESPN's abbreviations (ABH, DIR, FAT, FAY, HAZ, KHA, KHO, RIY, SHA) except Al Faisaly: ESPN uses 'ALF'; 'FAI' used instead (jo-al-faisaly also uses FAI, and KHA is also bh-al-khaldiya's code; the validator does not require unique codes).",
    "Logos: TheSportsDB badges read from its Saudi-Arabian Pro League page (league 4668), the same in two separate reads; the Al Fateh and Al Khaleej team pages confirmed theirs. Every club sits in that Saudi league list, so none is a namesake (e.g. the UAE or Omani Al Shabab).",
    "apiFootballId left out for all 10: no page found showing their API-Football ids (api-football.com/coverage failed to load; dashboard.api-football.com/soccer/ids was refused / needs a login).",
    "Stadium names are the organiser's (spl.com.sa team list, English and Arabic). ESPN calls some by older names: Al-Shabab Club Stadium = SHG Arena (the same match, Al Riyadh v Al Taawoun 24 Oct, is 'SHG Arena' in the SPL schedule and 'Al-Shabab Club Stadium' on ESPN), Al Fateh Club Stadium (Al-Hofuf) = Maydan Tamweel Aloula, King Khalid Sport City Stadium, Al Majma'a Sport City Stadium, Al-Hazm Club Stadium. Arabic 'ميدان تمويل الأولى' read twice on spl.com.sa/ar/teams (one PDF read gave 'تموين', taken as a misread).",
    "Al Riyadh: spl.com.sa lists Prince Faisal bin Fahd Sports City, where it played at home on 21 and 28 Aug (ESPN) and in MW7 (SPL schedule). But the SPL schedule PDF puts its MW9 (v Al Hilal), MW11 (v Al Taawoun) and MW12 (v Al Qadsiah) home matches at SHG Arena, and ESPN agrees for MW11. If that continues, those fixtures need their own 'venue' op (or switch the default to SHG Arena).",
    "Abha: home is Prince Sultan bin Abdulaziz Sports City (spl.com.sa; ESPN 13 Aug, 25 Aug, 4 Sep; SPL schedule MW12), but MW8 (v Al Faisaly) and MW10 (v Al Kholood) are listed at Damac Club Stadium (ملعب نادي ضمك), Khamis Mushait (SPL schedule; ESPN calls the MW10 ground 'Damac Stadium'). Those two need their own 'venue' op.",
